Story: REFUNDS-S3
Title: Diagnostic Error Payload Sanitization for Refund Inquiries

User story:
As a security compliance officer, I want third-party diagnostics to strip request bodies from error payloads arising from refund status checks so that sensitive customer data never leaves the system boundary.

Acceptance criteria:
- Given an error occurring during a customer refund status inquiry starting on sprint day 1, when stack traces and error payloads are transmitted to third-party diagnostics, then the request bodies are completely stripped before leaving the system.
- Given internal agents or general support staff attempting to trigger or modify refund transactions through this error path, when the action is evaluated, then all non-customer user groups are refused.
- Given the error handling mechanism, when a failure occurs, then no internal support ticketing modifications or messaging system alterations are performed.

Technical notes:
- Strip request bodies from error payloads on the third-party diagnostics landing surface. Details: when stack traces and error payloads are transmitted to third-party diagnostics during a customer refund status inquiry starting on sprint day 1, the middleware interceptor must sanitize the payload; do not alter existing telemetry SDK initialization or invent new error reporting services, adhering strictly to the rule that stack traces and error payloads sent to third-party diagnostics are stripped of request bodies before they leave the system.
- Restrict access exclusively to customer user groups on the refund status error path. Details: when internal agents or general support staff attempt to trigger or modify refund transactions through this error path, the authorization guard must evaluate the user group and refuse all non-customer actors; do not modify support ticketing systems or add internal agent workflows, leaving ticket modifications out of scope.

Out of scope:
Automated refunds, payment reversals, transaction record modifications, direct support ticketing modifications, messaging systems, and internal agent workflows are completely out of scope.

Coder hint:
Implement the diagnostic payload sanitizer middleware to drop request bodies during customer refund status inquiry error handling while enforcing customer-only access.

Implement that slice. Stay on this branch. Do not merge to the default branch.